course: dictionary
lesson: 10408
title: A word with three prongs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trident is a spear with three sharp points, like a fork with three prongs. When you meet this word, look for the clue words around it. In «The new country chose old symbols, the trident and the hryvnia», the words «old symbols» tell you the trident is a picture or object that stands for something.
explain: The sentence also says the new country chose the trident. A country chooses a symbol to show who it is. So you can guess that a trident is an object a country uses as a badge of its identity. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: «the picture and the hryvnia» still makes sense.
explain: Some words have a meaning in one place and a different one in another. Trident is a spear in myths and history, but it is also the name of a missile system. The sentences around the word tell you which meaning is being used.
fact: A trident is a spear with three sharp points.
fact: In myths, Poseidon (Greek) and Neptune (Roman), the gods of the sea, carry a trident.
fact: The trident is on the coat of arms of Ukraine, where it is called «tryzub».
fact: Britannia, the symbol of Britain, also holds a trident.
fact: Trident is also the name of the UK's nuclear missile system.
exercise: What is a trident? | *A spear with three sharp points | A small boat with one sail | A fishing rod with a reel | A hat worn by kings
exercise: In myths, who carries a trident? | A baker in the village | *Poseidon, the Greek god of the sea | A dragon with wings | A knight in armour
exercise: Find and copy the word from «The new country chose old symbols, the trident and the hryvnia» that names a symbol the country chose. | promises | *trident | country | Budapest
test: Poseidon strikes the ground with his trident to make earthquakes. What does trident mean here? | A shiny stone | *A spear with three sharp points | A type of bird | A fishing net
test: The trident is on the coat of arms of Ukraine. What is a coat of arms? | *A picture badge that stands for a country | A shield used in battle | A special cloak for winter | A set of tools
exam: Which clue tells you that a trident has more than one point? | country | Poseidon | blue | *three
